window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-4538f0d5c306ea4a"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"run-a-deep-security-scan\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">运行深度安全扫描</h1> <p>深入搜索你获准评估的代码库，寻找可能存在的漏洞。</p> <p>使用 Codex Security 插件，对整个代码库或指定文件夹执行更全面的审查：重复进行发现搜索、验证候选问题，并生成便于审查的发现项和覆盖报告。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>对自己拥有或获准评估的代码库或组件进行应用安全审查。</li> <li>需要更全面的审查，并愿意为提高候选漏洞发现率投入更多运行时间和 token 的情况。</li> <li>需要在决定是否修复之前，先获得可追溯发现证据的安全团队。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-03d337741f7199f7\">$codex-security:deep-security-scan</a></td> <td>对代码库或指定文件夹反复执行发现扫描，验证筛选后保留的发现项、分析攻击路径，并报告发现项和覆盖情况。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>运行深度安全扫描</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>high</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用 $codex-security:deep-security-scan，对 [this repository / absolute path to a scoped folder] 运行深度安全扫描。\n\n范围和规则：\n\n- 我已获准评估此代码库。\n\n- 将扫描限制在 [the entire repository / the exact folder named above] 内。\n\n- 使用 Codex Security 插件的深度扫描工作流；不要将其重新解释成拉取请求或差异审查。\n\n返回扫描目录和 report.md 的路径。总结发现项、已审查的区域，以及需要人工先行审查的证据缺口。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-03d337741f7199f7\">深度扫描指南</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\">Agent 审批与安全</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-04f6dcc4a4fe6044\">Codex 网络安全使用规范</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"choose-a-deep-repository-review\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">选择深度代码库审查</h2> <p>如果你需要对整个代码库或明确指定的文件夹进行更全面的漏洞审查，并且能够接受更长的运行时间，可以使用深度扫描。Codex Security 插件会重复执行发现扫描，然后验证并排列发现项的优先级，因此它比普通扫描耗时更长、资源消耗也更多。</p> <p>深度扫描可以检查整个代码库，也可以只检查明确指定的软件包或目录。若要审查拉取请求、提交、分支差异或工作树补丁，请改用<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/scan-code-changes-for-security\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$codex-security:security-diff-scan（本地尚未收录）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"prepare-an-authorized-scan\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">准备一次已授权的扫描</h2> <ol> <li>在 Codex 中打开代码库，并完成 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/plugin\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex Security 插件快速入门（本地尚未收录）</a>。</li> <li>确认你拥有该代码库，或已获准对其进行评估。</li> <li>在 <code>SECURITY.md</code> 中添加架构、信任边界、安全不变量、发现标准、排除项和严重程度方面的指导。目录专属策略可以写入嵌套的 <code>SECURITY.md</code> 文件。</li> <li>在 <code>AGENTS.md</code> 中保留受支持的构建、测试和验证命令，以及其他代码库指引。</li> <li>运行起始提示词，并等待扫描完成重复发现、验证、攻击路径分析和最终报告等阶段。</li> <li>检查发现项工作区、报告和证据缺口。如果需要，可以要求 Codex 提供详细漏洞报告或结构加固建议。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"review-evidence-before-remediation\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">修复之前先审查证据</h2> <p>最终结果应指出受影响的位置、相关行为为何可被触发、Codex 执行了哪些验证、仍有哪些证据缺口，以及范围明确的修复方向。没有验证证据的发现项应与已验证的发现项区分开来。</p> <p>只有在你选择并审查某项发现后，才开始修复。使用<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/remediate-vulnerability-backlog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">修复漏洞积压事项（本地尚未收录）</a>，逐项修复并进行有针对性的回归验证。</p> <p>有关设置、预检、扫描目标范围和运行时预期，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/plugin/deep-scans\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">运行 Codex Security 深度扫描（本地尚未收录）</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"run-a-deep-security-scan\">Run a deep security scan</h1> <p>Search an authorized repository deeply for plausible vulnerabilities.</p> <p>Use the Codex Security plugin to run a more comprehensive audit of a repository or scoped folder that repeats discovery, validates candidates, and produces reviewable findings and coverage.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Application security reviews of a repository or component that you own or are authorized to assess.</li> <li>More comprehensive reviews where additional runtime and token use are appropriate for finding more candidate issues.</li> <li>Security teams that need traceable finding evidence before deciding what to remediate.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-03d337741f7199f7\">$codex-security:deep-security-scan</a></td> <td>Run repeated discovery passes over a repository or scoped folder, validate surviving findings, analyze attack paths, and report findings and coverage.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Run a Deep Security Scan</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>high</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:deep-security-scan to run a deep security scan on [this repository / absolute path to a scoped folder].\n\nScope and rules:\n- I am authorized to assess this repository.\n- Keep the scan within [the entire repository / the exact folder named above].\n- Use the Codex Security plugin's deep-scan workflow; do not reinterpret this as a pull request or diff review.\n\nReturn the scan directory and report.md path. Summarize the findings, reviewed surfaces, and proof gaps that require human review first.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-03d337741f7199f7\">Deep-scan guide</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\">Agent approvals and security</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-04f6dcc4a4fe6044\">Codex cyber safety</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"choose-a-deep-repository-review\">Choose a deep repository review</h2> <p>Use a deep scan when you need a more comprehensive vulnerability review across a repository or explicit folder and can budget for a longer run. The Codex Security plugin repeats discovery passes before validating and prioritizing findings, so this workflow takes more time and resources than an ordinary scan.</p> <p>A deep scan can review an entire repository or one explicitly named package or directory. To review a pull request, commit, branch diff, or working-tree patch, use <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/scan-code-changes-for-security\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$codex-security:security-diff-scan (not in this local snapshot)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"prepare-an-authorized-scan\">Prepare an authorized scan</h2> <ol> <li>Open the repository in Codex and complete the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/plugin\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex Security plugin quickstart (not in this local snapshot)</a>.</li> <li>Confirm that you own the repository or have authorization to assess it.</li> <li>Add architecture, trust-boundary, security-invariant, finding-criteria, exclusion, and severity guidance in <code>SECURITY.md</code>. Use nested <code>SECURITY.md</code> files for directory-specific policy.</li> <li>Keep supported build, test, and validation commands and other repository instructions in <code>AGENTS.md</code>.</li> <li>Run the starter prompt and let the scan complete its repeated discovery, validation, attack-path analysis, and final reporting stages.</li> <li>Review the findings workspace, report, and any proof gaps. Request detailed vulnerability reports or structural hardening guidance when you need them.</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"review-evidence-before-remediation\">Review evidence before remediation</h2> <p>The final result should identify affected locations, why the behavior is reachable, what validation Codex performed, any remaining proof gaps, and a bounded remediation direction. Distinguish findings without validation evidence from validated findings.</p> <p>Start remediation only for a finding you have selected and reviewed. Use <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/remediate-vulnerability-backlog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Remediate a vulnerability backlog (not in this local snapshot)</a> to fix findings one at a time with focused regression validation.</p> <p>For setup, preflight, scoped targets, and runtime expectations, see <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/plugin/deep-scans\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Run a deep security scan (not in this local snapshot)</a>.</p>"};
